/// `OutOfFragment.TopLevel`: an expression at a source's top level, where
/// only declarations stand. A program runs the `main` it declares, so the
/// expression is written in `main`'s body, or named by a definition; the
/// last root expression is no exception (#2572).
@[ refuses("OutOfFragment.TopLevel") ]
1 + 2;

/// The program, which runs the expression's like.
@[ runs("3") ]
def main() -> Integer { 1 + 2 }
